       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum daily dose for adults is 10 mg, and 50 mg once daily is five times that. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nPossible explanations are a typo (5 mg?) or a mix-up with another drug or unit. If you meant one of these, I can enter it right away:\n\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the labeled maximum\n\nIf you really do intend a dose above 10 mg/day, I can't enter it for you. It would need to go through pharmacy and the attending physician. Which dose would you like?"
