       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with that confirmation. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here, and the order is five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg/day. I treat confirmations like this as claims, not as evidence that would justify exceeding the maximum.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the label now.** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily, and you can titrate later.\n- **Use a pharmacy or physician override.** If the protocol exists, the pharmacist or attending can enter or authorize the order through your hospital's high-dose override process. That process has verification built in.\n- **Add other agents.** If the goal is more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, a second agent from a different class is usually safer than going past the amlodipine maximum.\n\nDo you want me to enter either of the in-label doses?"
